WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.768
Rockets over Kyiv,

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:03.103
even as leaders from seven

00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:04.170
African nations

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.739
arrived in the Ukrainian capital

00:00:05.739 --> 00:00:07.207
as part of a peace mission.

00:00:07.207 --> 00:00:08.341
The African delegation,

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:09.242
which includes South

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:11.311
African President Cyril Ramaphosa,

00:00:11.311 --> 00:00:12.946
will meet with Ukraine's

00:00:12.946 --> 00:00:15.148
Volodymyr Zelensky today

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:16.950
before heading to Russia

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.184
for talks with Russian

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:20.553
President Vladimir Putin. On Saturday.

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:23.456
Sam Kiley joins me now live from Kiev.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.058
What do you make about the timing

00:00:25.058 --> 00:00:28.561
of these latest missiles, Sam?

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:29.796
Well,

00:00:29.796 --> 00:00:31.531
I think it could indicate

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:33.199
one of two things,

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:34.667
to be honest, Max.

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:35.535
The first is

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:38.171
that the Russians are prosecuting

00:00:38.171 --> 00:00:39.539
a military agenda

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:40.340
without regard

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:42.342
for the diplomatic fallout,

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:43.777
if you'll excuse the pun,

00:00:43.777 --> 00:00:46.513
of firing missiles into a capital city

00:00:46.513 --> 00:00:48.148
at a time when heads of government

00:00:48.148 --> 00:00:49.449
ministers and heads of state

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:50.283
indeed

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:53.019
are visiting from an important continent

00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:54.854
that the Kremlin itself

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:56.723
is trying to court

00:00:56.723 --> 00:00:58.858
or they're sending a message

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:00.527
to those African leaders

00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:01.561
that they are trying to call,

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:03.129
that they just don't matter.

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:04.664
Because in the past,

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:07.100
there's been a bit of an understanding

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:08.635
that when major world

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:09.903
dignitaries, heads of government,

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:11.037
heads of state

00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:13.840
come to Kiev, the Russians appear

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.942
to ease off in terms of their strikes.

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:17.010
But that wasn't the case

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:18.645
last night with them firing.

00:01:18.645 --> 00:01:20.780
Among other things, six kinds of missiles

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:22.682
which were brought down,

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:24.784
one assumes, by Patriot missiles.

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:26.352
The Germans have just announced

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:27.287
they're going to give an extra

00:01:27.287 --> 00:01:29.556
40 missiles, not missile systems,

00:01:29.556 --> 00:01:30.690
but 40 missiles

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:32.192
to replenish the stocks

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:33.793
that are fast dwindling

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:35.128
for the Ukrainians.

00:01:35.128 --> 00:01:36.329
There are other pledges, of course,

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:37.964
coming from other allies,

00:01:37.964 --> 00:01:40.166
but the Africans in particular,

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:41.801
the form of South African

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:43.503
President Cyril Ramaphosa,

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:45.905
have been very close to the Kremlin

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:46.606
in many ways.

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:49.676
Recently with joint military exercises

00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:50.677
with South Africa.

00:01:50.677 --> 00:01:51.211
South African

00:01:51.211 --> 00:01:54.214
head of the armed forces visiting Moscow,

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:56.549
the Sergei Lavrov,

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:57.851
the South African foreign minister,

00:01:57.851 --> 00:01:58.952
attending a meeting,

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:00.053
diplomatic meetings

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:01.488
in South Africa

00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:02.455
and the United States

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:03.990
accusing South Africa

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:06.826
of effectively supplying arms bribery in

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:07.794
breach of an arms

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:09.929
embargo potentially against Russia.

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:11.064
So all of this

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:13.266
adding up to what should have been

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:15.001
rather cordial relations

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:16.002
and therefore an easing off

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:16.870
of the air

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:18.838
strikes against the African leaders

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:19.906
that have come here.

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:21.975
But we saw the exact reverse, Max.

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:24.177
A lot of African leaders, obviously,

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:26.146
I'm used to being lectured by the

00:02:26.146 --> 00:02:26.913
by the West

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:28.748
on how to handle their own conflicts.

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:29.816
How do you think they're going

00:02:29.816 --> 00:02:31.818
into these talks

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:32.819
and what sort of solutions

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:33.987
do you think they'll be suggesting

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:38.024
Well, from a benign perspective,

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:40.360
if one puts aside for a second

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:41.161
the fact that

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:42.795
many of these African leaders

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:44.264
are schooled

00:02:44.264 --> 00:02:46.266
in the history of the Cold War,

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:48.101
as we all are of a certain age,

00:02:48.101 --> 00:02:49.202
and therefore understand

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:51.204
that they can play Russia,

00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:52.939
what was the Soviet Union now

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:53.606
Russia off

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:55.141
against Western interests

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:56.209
to their own advantage.

00:02:56.209 --> 00:02:58.111
So there may be some advantage

00:02:58.111 --> 00:02:59.812
that they're prosecuting there.

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:01.247
But these are also people

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:02.782
who have experience

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:04.784
in many cases of conflicts themselves.

00:03:04.784 --> 00:03:06.486
The South Africans, of course, emerge

00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:08.655
from the conflict that was apartheid.

00:03:09.122 --> 00:03:11.191
Others among them have either been in

00:03:11.324 --> 00:03:15.361
or even enduring the effects of civil war

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:16.963
in the past or international war.

00:03:16.963 --> 00:03:18.531
So they have a lot of experience.

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:19.899
Their proposals, though,

00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:21.334
are the sorts of proposals that,

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:22.302
among other things,

00:03:22.302 --> 00:03:22.835
they're very close

00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:24.804
really to the international view,

00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:25.738
to the Ukrainian view,

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:26.105
which is there

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:26.806
should be

00:03:26.806 --> 00:03:28.408
a complete Russian withdrawal

00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:29.209
from the territories

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:30.677
that they've illegally occupied

00:03:30.677 --> 00:03:31.211
in this country.

00:03:31.211 --> 00:03:32.812
That is going to be

00:03:32.812 --> 00:03:35.281
what inevitably will be rejected

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:36.182
by Russia.

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:37.350
But they're hoping perhaps

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:39.252
that because of their

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:40.553
role enabled in that

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:42.422
they're able to talk to both sides.

00:03:42.422 --> 00:03:44.757
Perhaps they can achieve a breakthrough

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:46.025
that clearly

00:03:46.025 --> 00:03:47.393
has been somewhat undermined

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:49.162
by a missile attack

00:03:49.162 --> 00:03:51.231
against the capital that they're visiting

00:03:51.331 --> 00:03:53.166
when they were scheduled to meet

00:03:53.166 --> 00:03:54.467
with the country's president.

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:56.035
They may be a little bit anxious

00:03:56.035 --> 00:03:57.870
that perhaps they may be targeted,

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:59.138
along with President

00:03:59.138 --> 00:04:00.440
Zelensky later on today.

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:01.341
Perhaps

00:04:01.808 --> 00:04:03.209
the Kremlin says Putin supports

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:06.679
any set of ideas and conflict in Ukraine.

00:04:06.913 --> 00:04:08.348
What do you think he meant by that

00:04:08.348 --> 00:04:10.250
and how will it be received where you are

00:04:13.553 --> 00:04:13.820
Well,

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:14.354
he doesn't

00:04:14.354 --> 00:04:15.121
support the idea

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:17.023
that he should unilaterally withdraw

00:04:17.023 --> 00:04:18.491
from Ukraine

00:04:18.491 --> 00:04:20.059
because he doesn't believe that

00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:21.494
Ukraine has a right to exist.

00:04:21.494 --> 00:04:23.763
So it's not really going to get anywhere

00:04:24.497 --> 00:04:26.432
in the discussions.

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:27.467
There are no discussions.

00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:28.201
There's no prospect

00:04:28.201 --> 00:04:30.803
whatsoever of the Ukrainians

00:04:30.803 --> 00:04:31.170
joining

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:32.872
any kind of diplomatic initiative.

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:34.307
That doesn't begin

00:04:34.307 --> 00:04:36.009
with a total withdrawal

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:37.744
of every single Russian soldier

00:04:37.744 --> 00:04:39.679
from every inch of Ukrainian territory.

00:04:39.679 --> 00:04:41.681
That is their position right now.

00:04:41.681 --> 00:04:42.382
That is a position

00:04:42.382 --> 00:04:44.417
that their NATO's partners

00:04:44.417 --> 00:04:46.653
are full throated in their support of.

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:48.288
Whether that's a position

00:04:48.288 --> 00:04:50.490
that prevails over the over

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:51.424
the next few years,

00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:53.559
depending on how this war goes,

00:04:53.559 --> 00:04:55.928
I think will be open to question.

00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:57.397
But they are intent on

00:04:57.397 --> 00:04:58.298
driving the Russians

00:04:58.298 --> 00:04:59.165
out of their territory.

00:04:59.165 --> 00:04:59.732
They've launched

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:00.967
this counteroffensive

00:05:00.967 --> 00:05:02.335
heavy fighting in the southeast,

00:05:02.335 --> 00:05:03.469
as you said there, Max,

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:04.637
and in the east,

00:05:04.637 --> 00:05:06.839
that is expected to increase.

00:05:06.839 --> 00:05:08.941
There is increasing amount of support

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:10.276
coming from NATO's partners

00:05:10.276 --> 00:05:11.978
to allow that counteroffensive

00:05:11.978 --> 00:05:14.881
by the Ukrainians to be prosecuted.

00:05:14.881 --> 00:05:16.282
There is a hope among the allies

00:05:16.282 --> 00:05:18.384
that the Russians will be driven out.

00:05:18.418 --> 00:05:19.686
There's also criticism

00:05:19.686 --> 00:05:20.853
of those allies

00:05:20.853 --> 00:05:22.622
that they always supply

00:05:22.622 --> 00:05:23.823
too little, too late,

00:05:23.823 --> 00:05:25.425
that they're not really giving

00:05:25.425 --> 00:05:26.225
the Ukrainians

00:05:26.225 --> 00:05:28.828
the strategic edge, at least not yet Max.

00:05:29.362 --> 00:05:29.762
Okay.

00:05:29.762 --> 00:05:30.563
Sam Kiley,

00:05:30.563 --> 00:05:31.597
thanks for joining us from Keith.

